        "tls": {
          "server_name": "*.<redacted-host>"
        }
      },
      "upstreams": [
        {
          "dial": "our-dial.com:30190"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
]
```

2. When a second node connects to the network (e.g. ID `123456`), we automatically call `upsert_route()` again to update our caddy master server so it serves a reverse_proxy to the node through the subdomain  `*.<redacted-host>`. Then, if we `GET` the handlers using the caddy admin API, we'll get something like this (handlers for nodes `982998` and `123456`) :

